@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Host mode contract model
+
+This isolated Python model belongs to AOSP Integration, not ASTER's detector.
+It is not installed, linked into Android, or a replacement for production tests.
+It exercises the proposed mode matrix before changes to report/classification,
+Framework persistence, notification rebinding and publication coordination.
+
+Run from the source root:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B system/core/libplatform_integrity_host/tests/mode_model/test_model.py
+python3 -B system/core/libplatform_integrity_host/tests/mode_model/test_shutdown.py
+```
+
+Inputs represent **already authenticated, parsed evidence**. Identity labels,
+baseline verification and capability flags in this model do not implement
+cryptographic verification, protocol parsing or resident-code measurement.
+`union` denotes the exact official-plus-approved-community reference set; it
+does not denote a same-name digest waiver. `endpoints_stopped` represents the
+stop confirmation needed at the tested authorization/recovery boundary.
+
+The model separates current findings, host retention, proc availability and
+positive permits. Normal-mode failure has no extra host latch; raw evidence
+may still prevent recovery. Compromise retention survives clean observations
+and reboot and clears only after a verified, persisted exit. An incomplete
+V4 observation receives a diagnostic ACK at most, never a clean publication
+or positive permit. Scalar faults are never fabricated as module names.
+
+Each new authority/endpoint instance requires explicit fresh binding; old
+notification proofs and late receipts cannot silently restore authorization.
+The model uses immutable plans as abstract exact request/receipt bindings,
+not as proof that the production transport already meets this contract.
+
+Limits: no concurrent runtime, actual fsync/crash recovery, SELinux, syscalls,
+kernel lifetime, proc byte-format/order proof, legacy-record migration,
+suspend timing or power tests. The ten-name projection only tests capacity,
+not the final evidence-order algorithm. Storage failures model failed commits;
+in-memory retention remains restrictive until a durable retry/recovery.
+The 104 early records are represented as incomplete coverage, not 104 module
+versions accepted by this model. Existing production behavior is unchanged.
+
+The shutdown interleaving model covers revocation, final observation/receipt,
+durable denial, expected close, timeout and process/boot boundaries. Its storage
+and receipt inputs are abstract barriers, not execution of AtomicFile, the
+property service, actual shutdown or hardware release. Production integration
+and device acceptance must be checked separately.
